    {
      "id": "def-gr-fx-bianchi-i-data",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "/root, adopting the named delegated complete-source semantic worksheet",
      "reason": "Released complete-source/eight-case worksheet research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step2-boundary-proposal-1/proposal.json: The Bianchi I datum fixes precisely three spatial indices i=1,2,3 on a nonempty time interval and four spacetime indices 0,1,2,3. The displayed sums have those fixed nonempty index sets; an empty-dimensional metric is outside this datum. Exact current Definition scope: Let $c>0$ be a fixed conversion constant in metres per second. Let $I\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval of physical time in seconds, and let $\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}=\\mathbb R^3/(2\\pi\\mathbb Z)^3$ have dimensionless angular coordinates $x^1,x^2,x^3$. Its quotient charts are local lifts to $\\mathbb R^3$; chart changes are translations by elements of $(2\\pi\\mathbb Z)^3$. Give $M=I\\times\\mathbb T^3_{2\\pi}$ the product smooth structure, so $M$ is a smooth four-manifold without boundary. Here a **$C^2$ time-oriented Lorentzian metric datum** means a symmetric covariant $2$-tensor field $g$ with $C^2$ components in smooth charts, whose value at each point has inertia $(3,1,0)$, together with a smooth vector field $N$ satisfying $g(N,N)<0$ everywhere. This is the explicit $C^2$ variant of the pointwise signature and time-orientation conditions in [[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]]; that supplier's metric regularity itself is smooth. . Root adopts and binds this actual semantic disposition to the current item and row; this is not independent proof acceptance."
    },
    {
      "id": "def-gr-fx-bianchi-i-curvature",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "/root, adopting the named delegated complete-source semantic worksheet",
      "reason": "Released complete-source/eight-case worksheet research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step2-boundary-proposal-8/proposal.json: The Bianchi I datum fixes precisely three spatial indices i=1,2,3 on a nonempty time interval and four spacetime indices 0,1,2,3. The displayed sums have those fixed nonempty index sets; an empty-dimensional metric is outside this datum. The item defines C2 connection and curvature arrays in translation-related Bianchi quotient charts, without a general low-regularity equivalence theorem. Exact current Definition scope: For a diagonal Bianchi I datum, use local quotient coordinates $x^0=t,x^1,x^2,x^3$, with indices $a,b,c,d\\in\\{0,1,2,3\\}$, and let $(g_{ab})$ and $(g^{ab})$ be the displayed metric matrix and its inverse. At this $C^2$ regularity, define\n\n$$\\Gamma^a{}_{bc}:=\\frac12g^{ad}\\bigl(\\partial_bg_{dc}+\\partial_cg_{bd}-\\partial_dg_{bc}\\bigr),$$\n\n$$R^a{}_{bcd}:=\\partial_c\\Gamma^a{}_{db}-\\partial_d\\Gamma^a{}_{cb}+\\sum_{e=0}^3\\bigl(\\Gamma^a{}_{ce}\\Gamma^e{}_{db}-\\Gamma^a{}_{de}\\Gamma^e{}_{cb}\\bigr),$$\n\n$$\\operatorname{Ric}_{bd}:=\\sum_{a=0}^3R^a{}_{bad},\\qquad \\mathcal R:=\\sum_{b,d=0}^3g^{bd}\\operatorname{Ric}_{bd},\\qquad G_{ab}:=\\operatorname{Ric}_{ab}-\\frac12\\mathcal R\\,g_{ab},\\qquad G^a{}_b:=\\sum_{c=0}^3g^{ac}G_{cb}.$$\n\nRepeated upper and lower indices in the first two displays are summed over $\\{0,1,2,3\\}$. The first formula gives coefficients symmetric in $b,c$ and, by expansion,\n\n$$\\Gamma^d{}_{ca}g_{db}+\\Gamma^d{}_{cb}g_{ad}=\\frac12(\\partial_cg_. Root adopts and binds this actual semantic disposition to the current item and row; this is not independent proof acceptance."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-gr-fx-bianchi-i-curvature-components",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "/root, adopting the named delegated complete-source semantic worksheet",
      "reason": "Released complete-source/eight-case worksheet research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step2-boundary-proposal-4/proposal.json: The Bianchi I datum fixes precisely three spatial indices i=1,2,3 on a nonempty time interval and four spacetime indices 0,1,2,3. The displayed sums have those fixed nonempty index sets; an empty-dimensional metric is outside this datum. Actual argument: Fixed3spatialscale factors positiveC2,c>0, finitecomponentcalculation. H_i=dotH_i=0 givesallcurvaturezero. Isotropic factors or somevanishingH_i allowed,no divisionbyH_i; openI hasnoendpointclaim. Exact current Statement scope: For a diagonal Bianchi I datum, write $H_\\Sigma:=H_1+H_2+H_3=3H$. In every local quotient chart, the only nonzero Christoffel symbols are $\\Gamma^0{}_{ii}=a_i^2H_i/c^2$ and $\\Gamma^i{}_{0i}=\\Gamma^i{}_{i0}=H_i$. The possibly nonzero lowered curvature components are exactly those obtained from the following values by the displayed sign reversals:\n\n$$R_{0i0i}=R_{i0i0}=-a_i^2(\\dot H_i+H_i^2),\\qquad R_{0ii0}=R_{i00i}=a_i^2(\\dot H_i+H_i^2),$$\n\n$$R_{ijij}=R_{jiji}=\\frac{a_i^2a_j^2}{c^2}H_iH_j,\\qquad R_{ijji}=R_{jiij}=-\\frac{a_i^2a_j^2}{c^2}H_iH_j\\quad(1\\le i<j\\le3).$$\n\nThe Ricci components are\n\n$$\\operatorname{Ric}_{00}=-\\sum_{i=1}^3(\\dot H_i+H_i^2),\\qquad \\operatorname{Ric}_{ii}=\\frac{a_i^2}{c^2}(\\dot H_i+H_iH_\\Sigma),$$\n\nand every off-diagonal Ricci component is zero.. Root adopts and binds this actual semantic disposition to the current item and row; this is not independent proof acceptance."
    },
    {
      "id": "prop-gr-fx-kasner-vacuum",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "/root, adopting the named delegated complete-source semantic worksheet",
      "reason": "Released complete-source/eight-case worksheet research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step2-boundary-proposal-6/proposal.json: The Bianchi I datum fixes precisely three spatial indices i=1,2,3 on a nonempty time interval and four spacetime indices 0,1,2,3. The displayed sums have those fixed nonempty index sets; an empty-dimensional metric is outside this datum. Exact current Statement scope: Let $a_i(t)=A_i(t/t_0)^{p_i}$ on a nonempty open interval $I\\subseteq(0,\\infty)$, where $A_i>0$ are lengths in metres, $t_0>0$ is a time in seconds, and $p_i\\in\\mathbb R$ are dimensionless exponents. These $p_i$ are called Kasner exponents for this power-law branch; define their sums $P:=\\sum_{i=1}^3p_i$ and $Q:=\\sum_{i=1}^3p_i^2$. For a nonstatic datum, meaning that not all $p_i$ vanish, the geometric vacuum equation $\\operatorname{Ric}=0$ in the $C^2$ curvature definition of this page holds exactly when $P=Q=1$. If all $p_i=0$, then the full curvature tensor vanishes, so the metric is flat in the curvature sense. These are exact statements about the specified finite-dimensional metrics; no singularity or generic cosmological conclusion follows.. Root adopts and binds this actual semantic disposition to the current item and row; this is not independent proof acceptance."
    },
