      "by": "/root, adopting the named delegated complete-source semantic worksheet",
      "reason": "Released complete-source/eight-case worksheet research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step2-boundary-proposal-4/proposal.json: The finite geometric sum ranges from r=0 through N with N nonnegative, so it always contains its identity term. The fixed spectral-band input is not an arbitrary family with an empty indexing option. Actual argument: An exact finite geometric identity is restricted to the closed spectral band and bounded by its scalar supremum; Cauchy–Schwarz gives the action remainder. Validity is for all E≥0, usefulness only E<M. Exact current Statement scope: Assume the hypotheses and notation of the positive heavy-mode Gaussian matching data. Let $E\\ge0$ be an energy and let $P_E:=E_A([0,E^2])$ be the spectral projection of $A$. For $J=P_EJ\\in H$ and an integer $N\\ge0$, define\n$$S_NJ:=M^{-2}\\sum_{r=0}^{N}(-A/M^2)^rJ,$$\nwhich is well-defined since $J$ has bounded spectral support. Put $R_NJ:=K^{-1}J-S_NJ$. Then\n$$\\|R_NJ\\|\\le M^{-2}(E^2/M^2)^{N+1}\\|J\\|,$$\nand\n$$\\left|\\Delta S_{\\mathrm{eff}}(J)+\\tfrac12\\langle J,S_NJ\\rangle\\right| =\\tfrac12|\\langle J,R_NJ\\rangle| \\le \\frac{\\|J\\|^2}{2M^2}(E^2/M^2)^{N+1}.$$\nUse natural units $\\hbar=c=1$: $A$ has units of mass squared, $E,M$ have mass units, and $E^2/M^2$ is dimensionless. Under the source normalization of the positive heavy-mode Gaussian matching data, $\\|J\\|^2/M^2$ and the action remainder are dimensionless. These are exact conditional bounds for every $E\\ge0$; the truncation is small/useful when $E<M$. No claim is made for unrestricted sources. Root adopts and binds this actual semantic disposition to the current item and row; this is not independent proof acceptance."
