      "reason": "Released complete-source/eight-case worksheet research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step2-boundary-proposal-5/proposal.json: The theorem requires n>=2 and a chosen basepoint in the nonempty configuration space. The curvature cancels by disjoint-slot commutation, diagonal Casimir invariance, and the Arnold identity. The based transport uses inverse monodromy for the library loop convention; full braid descent requires equal modules. Exact current Statement scope: Let $n\\ge2$, let $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex semisimple Lie algebra with Killing form $B$, let $V_i$ be finite-dimensional complex $\\mathfrak g$-modules, and let $\\kappa\\in\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\}$. Fix a basepoint $q\\in F_n(\\mathbb C)$. Let $D^2:=\\{z\\in\\mathbb C:|z|\\le1\\}$, $D^\\circ:=\\{z\\in\\mathbb C:|z|<1\\}$, $h(z):=z/(1+|z|)$, and $\\widetilde q:=(h(q_1),\\ldots,h(q_n))\\in F_n(D^\\circ)$. On $F_n(\\mathbb C)=\\{(z_1,\\ldots,z_n):z_i\\ne z_j\\text{ for }i\\ne j\\}$ let $\\nabla^{\\mathrm{KZ}}_\\kappa=d-\\kappa^{-1}\\sum_{i<j}\\Omega_{ij}\\eta_{ij}$ be the connection defined from the pairwise Casimir tensors $\\Omega_{ij}=\\sum_a\\rho_i(x_a)^{(i)}\\rho_j(x^a)^{(j)}$ and forms $\\eta_{ij}=(dz_i-dz_j)/(z_i-z_j)$, using $B$-dual bases. Then $\\nabla^{\\mathrm{KZ}}_\\kappa$ is flat. Its sheaf of local horizontal sections is a local system with right monodromy action $T$ of the fundamental group of the ordered configuration space based at $q$. With . Root adopts and binds this actual semantic disposition to the current item and row; this is not independent proof acceptance."
