      "case": "empty",
      "by": "/root, adopting the named delegated complete-source semantic worksheet",
      "reason": "Released complete-source/eight-case worksheet research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step2-boundary-proposal-5/proposal.json: The Statement assumes d≥1 and N≥3. The finite-state squared-jump formula counts each SSEP bond and has the N^-d gradient bound. Equal occupations and constant G give zero jumps, and t=0 has zero bracket. Exact current Statement scope: Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $d\\ge1$, $N\\ge3$, $T\\ge0$, and let $(\\eta_t)_{0\\le t\\le T}$ be the SSEP from the diffusive-model definition with any initial probability vector. For a real smooth periodic $G:\\mathbb T^d\\to\\mathbb R$, set\n\n$$M_t^{N,G}:=\\langle\\pi_t^N,G\\rangle-\\langle\\pi_0^N,G\\rangle-\\int_0^t\\langle\\pi_s^N,\\Delta_NG\\rangle\\,ds.$$\n\nThen $M^{N,G}$ is a square-integrable martingale. Its continuous predictable bracket is\n\n$$A_t^{N,G}=N^{2-2d}\\int_0^t\\sum_{i=1}^d\\sum_{x\\in\\Lambda_N}(\\eta_{x+e_i}(s)-\\eta_x(s))^2\\bigl(G((x+e_i)/N)-G(x/N)\\bigr)^2\\,ds,$$\n\nin the continuous predictable compensator convention of the finite-chain martingale supplier. In particular,\n\n$$A_T^{N,G}\\le T N^{-d}\\sum_{i=1}^d\\|\\partial_iG\\|_\\infty^2.$$. Root adopts and binds this actual semantic disposition to the current item and row; this is not independent proof acceptance."
